## Royal Asscher Diamond Price: What to Expect

The Royal Asscher Company does not publish a public price list. Prices vary by authorized dealer and negotiation. Based on current certified market data, these are the approximate ranges:

| Carat weight | Color/Clarity | Estimated range | Standard asscher comparison | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1ct | E-VS1 | ~$4,500–$6,500 | [$2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) standard | 40–80% premium over standard GIA equivalent |
| 1ct | D-VVS1 | ~$7,000–$10,000 | [$6,072](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/9160514?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) standard D-VVS2 | Premium narrows at top grades — standard D-VVS2 nearly overlaps |
| 2ct | E-VVS2 | ~$35,000–$45,000 | [$26,344](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/22977740?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) standard | $9,000–$19,000 brand gap at 2ct |
| 3ct | F-VVS2 | ~$65,000–$90,000 | [$36,991](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28507345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) standard | Premium exceeds $28,000 at 3ct — substantial brand tax |

**Verdict:** The premium grows with carat weight. At 1ct, you pay roughly $2,000–$4,000 more for the Royal Asscher brand. At 3ct, that gap exceeds $28,000. The diamond itself may be beautiful. But at $65,000+, you are paying a very large amount for a trademark on a stone you could get in a comparable grade at $36,991.

