## Royal Asscher vs Standard Asscher: Master Comparison Matrix

Use this to decide which is the right choice before buying.

| Factor | Standard Asscher | Royal Asscher | Winner | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Hall-of-mirrors depth | Full corridor effect | Partially reduced by extra facets | Standard | If you bought asscher for the corridors, standard delivers them better |
| Scintillation (sparkle) | Moderate, subdued | Higher, more active | Royal Asscher | Royal Asscher wins on sparkle — but not all asscher buyers want this |
| Price at 1ct E-VS1 | ~[$2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | ~$4,500–$6,500 | Standard | 40–80% premium for 16 extra facets and a laser inscription |
| Availability | Any major retailer | Royal Asscher Company + select dealers | Standard | Can't comparison-shop Royal Asscher — one vendor controls pricing |
| GIA cut grade | Not graded (vendor Ideal) | Not graded (vendor + brand cert) | Tie | Neither gets a GIA cut grade — both require manual proportion check |
| Resale value | Resale as commodity diamond | Resale loses brand premium fast | Standard | Brand premium disappears at resale — stone trades on GIA specs only |
| Lab option | Lab IGI from $2,795 | No lab version available | Standard | No lab Royal Asscher — if lab is an option, standard wins by default |
| Proprietary branding | None | Laser-inscribed, serial-numbered | Royal Asscher | Brand collectors value this — most buyers do not pay for it |
| History/legacy | 1902 original design | 2001 re-patented 74-facet version | Royal Asscher | Ironically, the standard asscher is closer to the original 1902 design |

**Verdict:** For most buyers, the standard asscher is the better value at every price point. The Royal Asscher is the right choice for a specific buyer: someone who specifically wants more sparkle than the standard asscher delivers, who values the brand story and the laser inscription, and who is not planning to resell. For everyone else, a proportion-verified standard asscher gives you 85–90% of the visual experience at 40–60% of the price.

