## Lab Grown Asscher: The Comparison Nobody Makes

The question most Royal Asscher buyers never ask: what does a lab-grown asscher D-IF cost at the same carat weight?

A Royal Asscher 1ct at approximately $4,500–$6,500 competes directly with lab IGI asscher stones that deliver D-IF clarity at significantly larger carat weights for less money. There is no lab version of the Royal Asscher — the company does not produce lab stones. But a well-cut lab asscher with verified proportions performs the same optical role at a fraction of the price.

[Asscher cut diamond proportions](/asscher-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions) are identical for lab and natural stones. A lab D-IF IGI asscher with depth 60–68%, table 60–68%, and Excellent symmetry produces the same hall-of-mirrors effect as the natural standard — at a lower price than a Royal Asscher of half the carat weight.

